#78250
"Icy Cavern"
"The walls of this narrow tunnel are entirely coated with sheets of thick,

shimmering ice.  Five-foot icicles hang like giant daggers from the ceiling.

A chilling wind blasts through the cave, churning sleet and ice into a

blinding dust that gluts the frigid air.  The tunnel heads north, and to the

south is a sort of cage formed of giant icicles that have grown all the way

down to the floor.

"
